# Agent memory — why and how things were decided

One file per fact. Frontmatter carries `name`, `description` and a `type`
(`user` / `feedback` / `project` / `reference`); the body states the fact and,
for feedback and project entries, **Why** and **How to apply**.

These files are the agent harness's persistent memory, committed here so the
reasoning behind decisions survives a lost server or session and is visible to
everyone. The `brief` CLI (see `.claude/rules/brief-cli-ops.md`) is not
installed on the GPU boxes, so on those the sync is a plain copy from the
harness directory `~/.claude/projects/<project>/memory/` into this folder,
committed with the work it documents. Newer wins; the harness copy is normally
newer.

